YOU MUST avoid creating large monolith files. If adding new functionality/features to an existing file, you MUST create a new file for the new functionality/features. If you're only updating existing functionality, you may add the edits to the existing file. But in general, prefer encapsulating new functionality/features in a new file to improve readability and maintainability.

docs/app-notes.txt describes the application

When testing locally, you are encouraged to use the `get_local_logs` MCP tool to view the logs of the local services.


### Operational Auditing
docs/attention.md is meant to hold any operational issues, contradictory instructions involved with coding and testing. Whenever you encounter these things, add a very concise note to the file. This includes things like:
    - instructions content tells you to run a script that doesn't exist or is in a different location than expected
    - a project doesn't build or run as expected according to the instructions
    - instructions content tells you to use a tool that is not capable of doing what is needed
    - You try to use a shell command that is not installed/available/doesn't work as expected